error[algo/equality-binding-invalid]: both sides of an equality bind new variables: left side binds variable `x`, right side binds variable `y`
   ┌─ algo/dataflow-bind-both-sides-of-equality.watsup:14:9
   │
14 │   -- if x = y
   │         ^^^^^
   │
   = An `=` premise reads as a comparison when both sides are already bound, or as a binder when one side is. With new variables on both sides it fits neither.

